<p>Use this menu to change the layout when printing, and to set 2 sided 
 printing.</p>
<p>Available functions differ depending on the printer or printer driver 
 you are using.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="default" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Restore Defaults</span></p>
<p>Restores the settings on this menu to the default settings.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="layout" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Layout:</span></p>
<p>Select the number of pages printed per sheet. Each document page to 
 be printed on a sheet will be placed in the order selected in the <span class="Term-Soft">Page Order:</span> list.</p>
<p><a href="~/Topics/IDH_HOW_LAYOUT">Printing Multiple Pages on a Sheet</a></p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="layoutorder" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Page Order:</span></p>
<p>Select a page layout when two pages or more per sheet is specified in 
 <span class="Term-Soft">Layout:</span>.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="drawborder" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Draw Border</span></p>
<p>Select the check box to print dotted separator lines for combined pages. 
 </p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="layoutmix" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Mixed Original Orientations...</span></p>
<p>When applying layout-printing to documents containing a mixture of landscape 
 and portrait pages, you can specify whether to print document pages whose 
 orientation differs from the paper orientation rotated by 90 degrees or 
 reduced in size without being rotated.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="2sided" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">2 sided:</span></p>
<p>Prints on both sides of sheets.<br/>
Specify how you want to open the bound output in the list.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="margins" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Binding Margins...</span></p>
<p>Open the <span class="Term-Soft">Binding Margins for 2 sided Printing</span> 
 dialog box, where you can specify the binding margins for 2 sided printing.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="booklet" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Booklet:</span></p>
<p>Prints output so that you can fold it into a booklet.</p>
<p>The pages of your document will be reduced in size and printed side 
 by side, two on each side of each sheet of the original paper size specified 
 in the application. For example, an A4 document will be printed as two 
 A5 images on each side of each A4 sheet.</p>
<p><a href="~/Topics/IDH_HOW_BOOKLET">Printing with a Layout Suitable for Making 
 Booklets</a></p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>There are only certain sizes of paper applicable 
 for this function.</p></li>
<li><p>To print at the same size as the original without 
 size reduction, select a paper size that is double that of the original 
 in the <span class="Term-Soft">Print On:</span> list on the <span class="Term-Soft">Basic</span> 
 menu.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Off</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Disables Booklet printing.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Magazine</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Two document pages are reduced and printed side 
 by side on each side of each sheet, and then the whole stack is folded 
 in half, like a magazine. </p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Mini Book</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Each sheet is folded in half separately, and then 
 the folded sheets are stacked and bound.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="bookletorder" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Page Order:</span></p>
<p>Select a page layout when <span class="Term-Soft">Magazine</span> or <span class="Term-Soft">Mini Book</span> is specified in <span class="Term-Soft">Booklet:</span>.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="bookletmix" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Mixed Original Orientations...</span></p>
<p>When applying booklet-printing to documents containing a mixture of 
 landscape and portrait pages, you can specify the imposition method.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="creep" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Creep Adjustment...</span></p>
<p>Prints the document with the creep adjustment function when <span class="Term-Soft">Magazine</span> 
 is selected in <span class="Term-Soft">Booklet:</span>.</p>
<p><a href="~/Topics/RPCS/IDH_HOW_CREEP">Using the Creep Adjustment Function</a></p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="nonreduction" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Do not [Fit to Print Size] auto.</span></p>
<p>Select the check box to print original-size documents side by side at 
 the center of the paper when <span class="Term-Soft">Magazine</span> is 
 selected in <span class="Term-Soft">Booklet:</span>.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="area" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Printable Area:</span></p>
<p>If the same document is printed on different printers and results in 
 a different number of pages being printed, adjust the printable area. 
 If you want to print over the whole page surface, select <span class="Term-Soft">Maximum</span>.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>The print inside the 5 mm (0.2 inches) margin 
 around the paper edges might be of reduced quality.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="adjust" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Set Image Position...</span></p>
<p>Click to open the <span class="Term-Soft">Set Image Position</span> dialog 
 box and then define the direction of the image position and the width 
 of the margins.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="blankpages" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Do not Print Blank Pages</span></p>
<p>Select the check box to leave blank pages unprinted.</p>
